# Smart Clinic Management System – User Stories

## 1. Admin User Stories

1. As an Admin, I want to log in securely so that I can access administrative features.
2. As an Admin, I want to add, update, and delete doctor profiles so that doctor information remains accurate.
3. As an Admin, I want to manage patient accounts so that patient records are maintained properly.
4. As an Admin, I want to view and manage appointments so that clinic operations run smoothly.
5. As an Admin, I want to manage user roles and permissions so that each user can access only authorized features.

## 2. Patient User Stories

1. As a Patient, I want to register and log in securely so that I can access my account.
2. As a Patient, I want to view available doctors so that I can choose a suitable doctor.
3. As a Patient, I want to book an appointment so that I can consult a doctor.
4. As a Patient, I want to view, reschedule, or cancel my appointments so that I can manage my schedule.
5. As a Patient, I want to view my medical history and prescriptions so that I can keep track of my healthcare information.

## 3. Doctor User Stories

1. As a Doctor, I want to log in securely so that I can access my dashboard.
2. As a Doctor, I want to manage my availability so that patients can book appointments during suitable time slots.
3. As a Doctor, I want to view my scheduled appointments so that I can plan my consultations.
4. As a Doctor, I want to access relevant patient medical records so that I can provide appropriate care.
5. As a Doctor, I want to create and manage prescriptions so that patients can follow their treatment plans.

## 4. Role-Based Access and Restrictions

- **Admin:** Can manage user accounts, doctor profiles, and clinic appointments.
- **Doctor:** Can manage availability, view assigned appointments, access authorized patient records, and manage prescriptions.
- **Patient:** Can manage their own profile and appointments and access their own medical history and prescriptions.

Each role must have appropriate permissions enforced by the backend to prevent unauthorized access to sensitive information.
